        <h2>Non-Silicone Release Agent Alternatives</h2>
        <p>Non-silicone release agent aerosols are formulated specifically to address the post-mold finishing limitations of silicone sprays. These alternative agents utilize active compounds such as synthetic waxes, heavy-duty fluoropolymers (PTFE), or biological lecithins. Because these active compounds do not possess the same spreading characteristics as silicones, they do not interfere with post-mold painting, printing, or adhesive bonding, allowing parts to bypass solvent washing steps.</p>
        <p>Fluoropolymer-based sprays establish a dry, chemical-resistant coating on the mold surface that is chemically inert and does not transfer to the molded part. This makes them highly effective for molding epoxies, urethanes, and other reactive thermoset resins. Wax-based release agents, while requiring more frequent application, are highly economical and form a robust barrier suitable for composite molding. Selecting the correct chemistry is vital for optimizing process efficiency and reducing scrap rates, as shown in the comparison table below.</p>

